	quest_links: [ ]
	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["210200000000000E"]
			description: [
				"&f&lFactory Logic.&r"
				""
				"Pipes solved &omoving&r things. They didn't solve &odeciding&r things."
				""
				"Every pipe you place is one more decision baked into the world - which side extracts, what it filters, where it goes. Change the plan and you re-wrench the whole wall."
				""
				"The four systems in this chapter replace that with something you can &oread&r: a program, a channel list, a logic expression, a flight plan. Write it once, change it in one place, and the base rearranges itself."
			]
			icon: "sfm:manager"
			id: "6AF9FD70EB5A15AB"
			rewards: [
				{
					count: 16
					id: "68EF088E3DD7DCAD"
					item: "minecraft:redstone"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "60080E309F6B2B65"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 50
				}
			]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "&7Stop wiring. Start writing."
			tasks: [{
				id: "3AA9EE5BD77273B7"
				title: "Decide to automate the deciding"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&bProgram the Base"
			x: -10.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6AF9FD70EB5A15AB"]
			description: [
				"&eSuper Factory Manager&r is the gentlest entry point in this chapter, and the most powerful thing here for the least effort."
				""
				"Place a &eManager&r, open it, and type something close to English:"
				""
				"&7EVERY 20 TICKS DO&r"
				"&7  INPUT FROM chest&r"
				"&7  OUTPUT TO furnace&r"
				"&7END&r"
				""
				"That's a working program. No cables to route by hand, no per-side config - the Manager reaches every inventory you've labelled."
			]
			icon: "sfm:manager"
			id: "3BF6BDC10CD08233"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6DDAC5176C8C61E6"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "&7Automation you can read back"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2EEDEA6E3C576EE8"
				item: "sfm:manager"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bThe Manager"
			x: -8.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3BF6BDC10CD08233"]
			description: [
				"The Manager needs to &osee&r the inventories it talks about. &eSFM Cable&r is how it reaches them - run it from the Manager to every chest, machine and tank you want in the program."
				""
				"Cable is cheap and dumb on purpose. It carries no items itself; it only extends the Manager's reach. All the intelligence stays in the one place you can actually edit."
			]
			icon: "sfm:cable"
			id: "47A7B0BFB116D2EB"
			rewards: [{
				id: "607523405A370BB1"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Reach, not throughput"
			tasks: [{
				count: 16L
				id: "129533685530B611"
