		{
			dependencies: ["6AF9FD70EB5A15AB"]
			description: [
				"&eIntegrated Dynamics&r is the deep end, and the most rewarding thing in this chapter if you stay with it."
				""
				"It isn't a pipe mod. It's a way to ask the world questions - &7how full is that tank&r, &7is this machine idle&r, &7does the ME system have 64 iron yet&r - and act on the answers."
				""
				"The &eLogic Programmer&r is where you build those questions out of operators, like assembling a formula. Start here; it explains itself better than any quest can."
			]
			icon: "integrateddynamics:logic_programmer"
			id: "5C273F0F3989D687"
			rewards: [{
				id: "751960C0870FA23A"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "&7Ask the world questions"
			tasks: [{
				id: "562E02AB00452ECD"
				item: "integrateddynamics:logic_programmer"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bThe Logic Programmer"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5C273F0F3989D687"]
			description: [
				"&eVariables&r hold the answers your Logic Programmer produces. A &eVariable Store&r keeps them somewhere the network can read."
				""
				"&eLogic Cable&r is the nervous system - it carries no items at all, only information, and every part you place later sits on it."
				""
				"Nothing visible happens yet. That's normal: you're building the wiring that the next two quests plug into."
			]
			icon: "integrateddynamics:cable"
			id: "054CDC18C3A87BDD"
			rewards: [{
